;; Companion to kotoba-native kernel-object-entries `aiueos-browser-frame2`
;; (guest browser desktop frame with text, ADR-0224).
;;
;; One list of rects AND glyphs, window by window in stack order. Every
;; success vector asserts the whole op list. The expected lists were produced
;; by a model written apart from the object (layout rules in the object
;; header), over a five-glyph fixture cut from os/aiueos/fonts/aiueos-16.fnt:
;; U+003F ? , U+0041 A, U+0061 a, U+3042 あ (16 px), U+FFFD. U+3041 ぁ is NOT
;; in the fixture, so it must come out as the U+FFFD glyph.
;;
;; SURFACE at :surface (8192 bytes): state words 0..31, titles at word
;; 32 + 32(id-1), bodies at 160 + 64(id-1), scratch 416..431, IME 432..479,
;; ops from word 480 (byte 1920), 24 bytes each: kind x y a b rgb (kind 2:
;; a = glyph index, b = width). `fourth-window-body-reads-all-64` pins the
;; 2026-09-24 overlap of the old scratch (400..415) with window 4's body.
;;
;; COMPOSITION (ADR-0227): the IME words 433 (romaji length), 434.. (romaji),
;; 445 (preedit length), 446.. (preedit) are drawn after the focused body,
;; each glyph with a 1 px rule at y + 17. The six `composition-*` /
;; `committed-*` vectors' op lists come from
;; os/aiueos/scripts/browser-frame-model.cljk --ops, the same model that
;; reproduces every older success vector here byte for byte and the three
;; census lines ADR-0224 / 0225 pinned on serial.
;;
;; CARET (ADR-0232): every success vector's list now ends the focused window
;; with a 1 x 16 #111111 rect at the cursor (kind 1, a = 1, b = 16), unless
;; its foot passes the bottom inset (`body-stops-at-the-bottom-inset`,
;; `composition-cut-at-the-bottom-inset` keep their old lists). The eleven
;; lists that changed were regenerated from the model, whose decoder first
;; reproduced all thirteen old lists from their seeds unchanged.
;;
;; LAUNCHER AND CLOSE (ADR-0233): word 31 is the app register. Every vector
;; above has it 0 and kept its list. The four `launcher-*` / `close-*` /
;; `*-40-wide-*` vectors set it: the launcher row and buttons right after the
;; background, a close control (16 x 16 #e4e8ef and U+00D7 -- the fixture has
;; no U+00D7, so its U+FFFD) after each title of a window at least 40 wide,
;; the title clipping 20 px earlier. Their lists come from
;; browser-frame-model.cljk --ops over the fixture font.
;;
;; BODY FLOW (ADR-0234): the body is laid out as browser.surface + cssom lay
;; out the window's document (the object header has the rule): text 14 in from
;; the body box (x, y + 28), lines w - 28 wide, white-space runs collapsed,
;; packed by words, each 10 a <br>. Every success vector's list changed (the
;; insets moved) and was regenerated by browser-frame-model.cljk --vectors,
;; which decodes each vector's seed and fixture -- and which, with the old body
;; rule put back, first reproduced all nineteen old lists byte for byte. The
;; eight `body-*` / `br-*` / `a-*` vectors take a six-glyph fixture that adds
;; U+0020 (the five-glyph one has no space, so its space is U+FFFD's 16 px):
;; a line exactly W and one a pixel past it, a body that fits keeping its
;; leading and trailing space, a body of white space only, <br> segments with
;; an empty one, a word overflowing the right edge, the viewport clip (glyphs
;; and caret), and W below 0. The body rules themselves are compared against
;; the hosted engine in browser-flow-parity-v1.edn, not here.
;;
;; POINTER (ADR-0236): word 2046 is the pointer's x + 1 (0 = none), 2047 its
;; y. Every vector above has 2046 = 0 and kept its list (the model, given the
;; pointer, first reproduced all 27 old lists from their seeds unchanged).
;; The four `pointer-*` success vectors end their list with the arrow -- 12
;; rows, an #111111 outline rect per row and a #ffffff fill in rows 2..10 --
;; over a window, cut at the right edge, cut at the bottom, and at the last
;; pixel (one rect); their lists come from browser-frame-model.cljk
;; --vectors. Three refusals (-10): x at vw, y at vh, y = 2^32 - 1.
;;
;; SCROLL (ADR-0238): words 2040..2043 are window id 1..4's vertical offset;
;; the body, composition and caret are drawn that much higher and cut at the
;; top inset y + 36 as at the bottom inset. Every vector above has the four
;; words 0 and kept its list. The op capacity is 260 (words 480..2039; it was
;; 261 and 2040..2045 were op 260's): `exactly-260-ops-are-drawn` and
;; `two-hundred-sixty-one-ops-are-refused` pin the edge. Nine more success
;; vectors (lists from browser-frame-model.cljk --vectors): both insets met
;; exactly (offset 6), one past the top (7), the composition and caret with
;; the offset, one window of two scrolled, offsets of windows not open, 65535,
;; the title and close control fixed. Two refusals (-11): 65536 and 2^32 - 1.
;;
;; SELECTION (ADR-0240): words 2036 (the window id) and 2037 (k) select the
;; last min(k, n) code points of that window's body when it is focused. Each
;; drawn glyph of a selected code point has, right before it, a rect of its
;; width, 16 high, #b5cdf1 (cssom sel-ops' rgba(70,130,220,0.4) over #ffffff);
;; there is no caret while something is selected. Every vector above has both
;; words 0 and kept its list (the model, given the selection, first reproduced
;; them from their seeds unchanged). The op capacity is 259 (words 480..2033,
;; the six words after it freed for the selection and one scratch word):
;; `exactly-259-ops-are-drawn` and `two-hundred-sixty-ops-are-refused` are the
;; two ADR-0238 edge vectors with one body code point less. Eleven success
;; vectors (lists from browser-frame-model.cljk --vectors): the highlight and
;; no caret; an empty selection of the focused window and Shift held (the
;; caret, nothing highlighted); another window's selection; k past the body;
;; a selected 10; a packed space with its word and without; a collapsed run's
;; space; a cut glyph; a scroll offset; the 64th code point.
